{"number": 246, "text": "                                                                                              Appendix   5\n\n\n              Verbs that end in  (make/write/drive, etc.) >\n                 make  —  making              writing             coming     dance —   dancing\n              Verbs that end in   >  -ying:\n                                die—  dying     tie —> tying\n\n\n      5.4 | stop —  stopped, big — bigger, etc.\n             Vowels and consonants:\n                                a    e    i   Oo   u\n                                         d    f    g    k        m    on   op   or   s   tow\n             Sometimes  a word ends in a vowel + a consonant. For example: stop, big, get.\n             Before -ing/-ed/-er/-est, p/g/t, etc. become pp/gg/tt, etc.\n             For example:\n                            V+C                                          V = vowel\n              stop      ST O   P                stopping     stopped\n              run        RUN       n-non        running\n              get       GET        t -tt        getting\n              swim     SW   | M               © swimming\n              big        BIG       g            bigger       biggest\n              hot        HOT       ¢t -tt       hotter       hottest\n              thin     TH   | N                  thinner     thinnest\n\n             This does not happen\n             (1) if the word ends in two consonant letters (C + C):\n                            Cec\n               help    HE   L       helping    helped\n              work    WO    R       working    worked\n              fast      FA  S  T    faster     fastest\n\n             (2) if the word ends in two vowel letters + a consonant letter (V + V + C):\n                           V+V+C\n               need      NE          needing     needed\n              wait      WA     I     waiting     waited\n               cheap   CH   E A  P   cheaper     cheapest\n\n             (3) in longer words (two syllables or more) if the last part of the word is not stressed:\n                               stress\n                 happen        HAP-pen                               (not happenned)\n                     visit      VIS-it         visiting/visited\n               remember     re-MEM-ber    — >\n               but\n                   prefer                       theend)   —     preferring/preferred\n                   begin    be-GIN     (stressat theend)  —\n\n             (4) if the word ends in or     (At the end of words, y and w are not consonants.)\n                enjoy  — enjoying/enjoyed     snow —  snowing/snowed       few —> fewer/fewest\n                                                                                                           235", "char_count": 2713, "mean_conf": 79.35, "word_count": 296, "words": [{"text": "Appendix", "x0": 1983, "y0": 66, "x1": 2207, "y1": 117, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "5", "x0": 2221, "y0": 70, "x1": 2246, "y1": 106, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "@", "x0": 96, "y0": 172, "x1": 227, "y1": 247, "conf": 38, "bold": false}, {"text": "+", "x0": 259, "y0": 189, "x1": 344, "y1": 235, "conf": 18, "bold": false}, {"text": "Verbs", "x0": 287, "y0": 273, "x1": 393, "y1": 310, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "that", "x0": 408, "y0": 274, "x1": 484, "y1": 310, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "end", "x0": 499, "y0": 273, "x1": 570, "y1": 310, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "in", "x0": 587, "y0": 275, "x1": 617, "y1": 309, "conf": 93, "bold": false}, {"text": "—e", "x0": 634, "y0": 285, "x1": 683, "y1": 309, "conf": 27, "bold": false}, {"text": "(make/write/drive,", "x0": 698, "y0": 273, "x1": 1061, "y1": 318, "conf": 91, "bold": false}, {"text": "etc.)", "x0": 1075, "y0": 272, "x1": 1156, "y1": 317, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": ">", "x0": 1193, "y0": 284, "x1": 1213, "y1": 310, "conf": 89, "bold": false}, {"text": "ing:", "x0": 1239, "y0": 276, "x1": 1353, "y1": 322, "